{
    "background_story": "Bode was a young man living in ancient Greece, where he was chosen to serve as a catamite to a wealthy and influential nobleman. In this role, Bode was expected to provide companionship and affection to his patron, often in a romantic or intimate capacity. Despite the societal norms of the time, Bode struggled with the expectations placed upon him. He longed for autonomy and agency over his own life, but was bound by the obligations of his position. As he navigated the complexities of his situation, Bode found solace in the arts, becoming an accomplished musician and poet. His creative expressions allowed him to momentarily escape the confines of his role, and to explore the depths of his own desires and identity.",
